1. What do all the methods (move(), special_move(), use()) in the previous activities have in common?
They all demonstrate polymorphism because they use the same method names but can perform different actions depending on the object.
2. How does this activity show polymorphism in a gaming context?
It shows polymorphism because different characters and items can perform different actions using the same method. For example, a Warrior uses a sword, while a Mage casts a spell. Different potions also have different effects when used.
3. Can you think of other examples where the same action behaves differently depending on the character or item?
Yes. An attack action can be different depending on the character. A Warrior attacks using a sword, an Archer shoots arrows, and a Mage uses magic. They all attack, but in different ways.